WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
The first practice function simply prints Hello.

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:07.632
It has no parameters, so every call does the same thing.

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:10.917
The second function adds a name parameter.

00:00:10.917 --> 00:00:14.652
Now the same function can greet different people or labels.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:19.680
Run both examples, then change the argument in the second function.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.721
Compare how much more flexible the parameterized version is.
